Every API response repeats these terms in its `license` object and in a
`Link: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>; rel="license"`
header, so an integration never has to go looking for them.

The catalogue exists because people read announcements from AMSAT, ARISS,
clubs and operators, and check them by hand before publishing. Attribution
is what sends the next reader back to that work, which is why it is a
condition of use and not a courtesy.

Where the data describes facts (a frequency, a date, a NORAD number),
those facts are not owned by anyone. What this licence covers is the
catalogue: the selection, the verification and the arrangement of them.
